  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nAn upper ridge over the western states is bringing the heat back\nto the area. The base NBM has 100 degrees forecast for at least a\nfew locations through Wednesday. Today, a shortwave trough is\nexpected to bring an isolated storm to the southwest and\nnortheast. The main concern is gusty outflow winds. A shortwave\ntrough is expected to move into the southwest part of the area\ntomorrow afternoon and evening, and the main concern is gusty\nwinds again. The base HREF has gusts up to around 60 mph, and the\nmaximum HREF has gusts up to 80 mph. There is a low probability of\n80 mph occurring tomorrow. The main concern for fire starts is low\nhumidity and strong winds for today, and lightning strikes\ntomorrow. There is a Red Flag Warning out for fire zones 122, 135,\n134, 137, and 136 for today, and fire zones 134, 135, 136, and 137\nfor tomorrow afternoon and evening.\n\nAbundant smoke from the Pacific NW fires is over the area, and\nmainly reducing visibility from 1 KM to 6 KM above the ground.\nThere is a chance of this haze and smoke affecting sensitive\ngroups near the ground for smoke that does reach the ground.\n\nWest winds are strong enough to support the Lake Wind Advisory\nfrom now through 6 PM this evening.\n\nThere is an Extreme Heat Warning in effect for this strong ridge\nthat has aided in bringing temperatures up. These warm conditions\nduring the day and poor temperature recoveries at night\n(temperatures staying above 65 degrees) will make it important to\nhave efficient cooling systems in place. These poor temperature\nrecoveries are in the forecast in the southern half of the area\nthrough Thursday.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nThe only deviation was to add a slight chance of PoPs to various\nparts of the area through tomorrow evening.\n\nThere is high confidence in the heat products that are in effect\nthrough Sunday evening. There is moderate confidence in heat\nproducts being needed again during the week.\n\nThere is low to moderate confidence in severe wind gusts occurring\nin the northeast this evening and in the west tomorrow afternoon \nand evening.\n\nThere is high confidence in smoke moving through the area from 1\nkilometer and 6 kilometer above the ground through tomorrow\nmorning, and moderate confidence in surface haze and smoke\noccurring.\n\nThere is high confidence in the Red Flag Warning verifying today,\nand moderate confidence for tomorrow. This confidence is the same\nfor the Lake Wind Advisory in effect for today.",
